website=f'''<section class="page-hero shell"><p class="eyebrow">WEBSITE DESIGN & CONNECTED CUSTOMER JOURNEYS</p><h1>A clearer website.<br>A better way to <em>start.</em></h1><p>Help the right person understand your service, trust the evidence, and take a useful next step. Then make sure that step reaches the right person in your business.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="/website-intake.html">Start my demo brief <span>→</span></a><a class="button secondary" href="#packages">Explore starting offers <span>↓</span></a></div></section><section class="section shell website-principles"><div><span>01 / CLEAR CONTENT</span><h2>Answer the questions<br>people actually have.</h2><p>What you do, who it fits, what they receive, what affects price and timing, and what happens next. Real information before more decoration.</p></div><div><span>02 / USEFUL CONNECTIONS</span><h2>Fit the business.<br>Keep it dependable.</h2><p>Use your existing scheduler, customer system, or payment provider when it fits. Add custom integration only when a real task needs it.</p></div><div><span>03 / CONFIDENT OWNERSHIP</span><h2>See it on test.<br>Know how to run it.</h2><p>A source repository, test and live sites, verified journeys, and a documented handoff and recovery path are part of the delivery plan.</p></div></section><section class="surface section" id="packages"><div class="shell"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">STARTING OFFERS FOR REVIEW</p><h2>Choose the scope<br>that fits the work.</h2></div><p>These are the existing test-site offers. Your written proposal confirms scope, providers, ongoing costs, and support.</p></div><div class="price-grid">{packhtml}</div><p class="fine-print">Third-party subscriptions, usage charges, commerce operations, and work beyond the agreed scope are confirmed separately. Hosting-only options start at $39/month for qualifying sites. No ranking or lead-volume guarantee.</p></div></section><section class="section shell split"><div><p class="eyebrow">ROOM FOR COMMERCE</p><h2>Ready for the right<br>kind of purchase.</h2></div><div><p>Need a deposit, consulting package, tutorial, or a few products? Start with a proven checkout service and a clear fulfillment process. Add a catalog and cart when your operation needs them.</p><p>Payments, appointments, and access are separate responsibilities. We define who owns each before adding a Buy button.</p></div></section><section class="section shell"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">COMMON QUESTIONS</p><h2>Before we start.</h2></div></div><div class="faq"><details><summary>Do I need to know which platform I want?</summary><p>No. We begin with your offer, customer journey, current tools, and editing needs. Then we recommend the smallest dependable architecture.</p></details><details><summary>Can you redesign an existing website?</summary><p>Yes. We inspect the current site and ownership first, preserve useful content and URLs, and plan redirects and cutover where needed.</p></details><details><summary>Can the site connect to booking or payments?</summary><p>Yes, when included in the scope. We select the provider and test the actual confirmation, follow-up, and recovery process.</p></details><details><summary>Will I own the domain and accounts?</summary><p>Our default is customer-controlled business accounts, with code and content rights documented in the agreement. We establish the handoff before provisioning.</p></details><details><summary>Is the first questionnaire a project commitment?</summary><p>No. It supplies the direction for discovery and an initial demo. We agree scope, costs, and publication separately.</p></details></div></section>{cta()}'''
(ROOT/'website-lift.html').write_text(page('Website design for small businesses','A clear service website with search foundations, booking and inquiry connections, test review, and a practical handoff.',website,'website-lift'))

workflow=f'''<section class="page-hero shell"><p class="eyebrow">THE RDC DELIVERY APPROACH</p><h1>Know the step.<br>See the <em>result.</em></h1><p>Our six delivery phases keep the work focused, reviewable, and ready for someone to own. Small fixes use a lighter version of the same discipline.</p><a class="button primary" href="/website-intake.html">Start with your website brief <span>→</span></a></section><section class="section shell"><div class="delivery-list">'''+''.join(f'<article><span class="delivery-number">0{i+1}</span><div><p class="eyebrow">{p[0]}</p><h2>{p[1]}</h2><p>{p[2]}</p></div><div class="delivery-output"><span>REVIEWABLE OUTPUT</span><strong>{p[3]}</strong></div></article>' for i,p in enumerate(phases))+f'''</div></section><section class="section surface"><div class="shell split"><div><p class="eyebrow">DELIVERY YOU CAN REVIEW</p><h2>A launch is a milestone.<br>Ownership is the finish.</h2></div><div><p>Controlled testing happens before the operational pilot. Real use and initial adoption happen before permanent ownership transfers.</p><p>At handoff, you know where the code lives, who controls the domain, how inquiries are handled, and how support and recovery work. Larger future needs return as a new scoped project.</p><a class="text-link" href="/portal/">Explore the delivery workspace →</a></div></div></section>{cta()}'''
(ROOT/'workflow.html').write_text(page('How RDC delivers websites and systems','Six delivery phases from discovery and test through operational pilot, launch, handoff, and ongoing improvement.',workflow,'workflow'))

